these crystals

2138
00:41:25,960 --> 00:41:26,960
called Charcol-Liden crystals

2139
00:41:26,960 --> 00:41:27,960
which again

2140
00:41:27,960 --> 00:41:29,960
are derived from eosinophils

2141
00:41:29,960 --> 00:41:30,960
and examiners love

2142
00:41:30,960 --> 00:41:32,960
to show pictures like this

2143
00:41:32,960 --> 00:41:33,960
the last thing I should say

2144
00:41:33,960 --> 00:41:34,960
about asthma

2145
00:41:34,960 --> 00:41:35,960
is that there are also

2146
00:41:35,960 --> 00:41:36,960
some non-allergic

2147
00:41:36,960 --> 00:41:37,960
causes of asthma

2148
00:41:37,960 --> 00:41:38,960
for example exercise

2149
00:41:38,960 --> 00:41:39,960
some patients will say

2150
00:41:39,960 --> 00:41:40,960
that exercise

2151
00:41:40,960 --> 00:41:41,960
gives them asthma

2152
00:41:41,960 --> 00:41:42,960
other patients might say

2153
00:41:42,960 --> 00:41:44,960
that a viral infection

2154
00:41:44,960 --> 00:41:45,960
would give them asthma

2155
00:41:45,960 --> 00:41:47,960
some patients will say

2156
00:41:47,960 --> 00:41:48,960
that when they go to work

2157
00:41:48,960 --> 00:41:49,960
they get exposed

2158
00:41:49,960 --> 00:41:50,960
to certain dust

2159
00:41:50,960 --> 00:41:51,960
and that causes asthma

2160
00:41:51,960 --> 00:41:52,960
so these are some

2161
00:41:52,960 --> 00:41:53,960
other causes of asthma

2162
00:41:53,960 --> 00:41:54,960
asthma is not always

2163
00:41:54,960 --> 00:41:55,960
allergic

2164
00:41:55,960 --> 00:41:57,960
one very high yield

2165
00:41:57,960 --> 00:41:58,960
cause of asthma

2166
00:41:58,960 --> 00:41:59,960
to be familiar with

2167
00:41:59,960 --> 00:42:00,960
is aspirin

2168
00:42:00,960 --> 00:42:01,960
now let me remind you

2169
00:42:01,960 --> 00:42:02,960
that there are

2170
00:42:02,960 --> 00:42:03,960
a subset of patients

2171
00:42:03,960 --> 00:42:04,960
I think it's like

2172
00:42:04,960 --> 00:42:05,960
ten to fifteen percent

2173
00:42:05,960 --> 00:42:06,960
of adult patients

2174
00:42:06,960 --> 00:42:07,960
with asthma

2175
00:42:07,960 --> 00:42:08,960
who have something called

2176
00:42:08,960 --> 00:42:09,960
aspirin intolerant asthma

2177
00:42:09,960 --> 00:42:10,960
so they have asthma

2178
00:42:10,960 --> 00:42:11,960
and that's the first part

2179
00:42:11,960 --> 00:42:12,960
of the triad

2180
00:42:12,960 --> 00:42:13,960
but they also have

2181
00:42:13,960 --> 00:42:14,960
this funny thing

2182
00:42:14,960 --> 00:42:15,960
where they actually get

2183
00:42:15,960 --> 00:42:16,960
bronchospasm

2184
00:42:16,960 --> 00:42:18,960
so that's a second feature

2185
00:42:18,960 --> 00:42:19,960
of this disease

2186
00:42:19,960 --> 00:42:20,960
it's aspirin induced

2187
00:42:20,960 --> 00:42:21,960
bronchospasm

2188
00:42:21,960 --> 00:42:22,960
and the third feature

2189
00:42:22,960 --> 00:42:23,960
is nasal polyps

2190
00:42:23,960 --> 00:42:24,960
and that's an interesting

2191
00:42:24,960 --> 00:42:25,960
feature

2192
00:42:25,960 --> 00:42:26,960
also seen in

2193
00:42:26,960 --> 00:42:28,960
aspirin intolerant asthma

2194
00:42:28,960 --> 00:42:29,960
let's just talk about

2195
00:42:29,960 --> 00:42:30,960
nasal polyps for a second

2196
00:42:30,960 --> 00:42:31,960
now nasal polyps

2197
00:42:31,960 --> 00:42:32,960
when you think about them

2198
00:42:32,960 --> 00:42:33,960
remember from

2199
00:42:33,960 --> 00:42:34,960
earlier in this chapter

2200
00:42:34,960 --> 00:42:35,960
that you know

2201
00:42:35,960 --> 00:42:36,960
you classically see

2202
00:42:36,960 --> 00:42:37,960
a nasal polyp

2203
00:42:37,960 --> 00:42:38,960
in a patient with

2204
00:42:38,960 --> 00:42:39,960
chronic rhinitis

2205
00:42:39,960 --> 00:42:40,960
which is inflammation

2206
00:42:40,960 --> 00:42:42,960
of the sinonasal mucosa

2207
00:42:42,960 --> 00:42:43,960
however there are some

2208
00:42:43,960 --> 00:42:44,960
other high yield associations

2209
00:42:44,960 --> 00:42:45,960
with nasal polyp

2210
00:42:45,960 --> 00:42:46,960
for example

2211
00:42:46,960 --> 00:42:47,960
an adult with nasal polyp

2212
00:42:47,960 --> 00:42:48,960
with asthma

2213
00:42:48,960 --> 00:42:49,960
like symptoms

2214
00:42:49,960 --> 00:42:50,960
you think about

2215
00:42:50,960 --> 00:42:51,960
aspirin intolerant asthma

2216
00:42:51,960 --> 00:42:52,960
so that's one

2217
00:42:52,960 --> 00:42:53,960
important association

2218
00:42:53,960 --> 00:42:54,960
another very high yield

2219
00:42:54,960 --> 00:42:55,960
association

2220
00:42:55,960 --> 00:42:56,960
is that if you have a child

2221
00:42:56,960 --> 00:42:57,960
like a two year old

2222
00:42:57,960 --> 00:42:58,960
with nasal polyps

2223
00:42:58,960 --> 00:42:59,960
what do you have to think about

2224
00:42:59,960 --> 00:43:01,960
cystic fibrosis

2225
00:43:01,960 --> 00:43:02,960
that's high yield

2226
00:43:02,960 --> 00:43:03,960
patients actually

2227
00:43:03,960 --> 00:43:04,960
who have nasal polyps

2228
00:43:04,960 --> 00:43:05,960
need to be tested

2229
00:43:05,960 --> 00:43:06,960
for cystic fibrosis

2230
00:43:06,960 --> 00:43:07,960
at that age

2231
00:43:07,960 --> 00:43:08,960
so that's another important

2232
00:43:08,960 --> 00:43:09,960
thing to be aware of

2233
00:43:09,960 --> 00:43:10,960
anyway that concludes

2234
00:43:10,960 --> 00:43:11,960
our discussion of asthma

2235
00:43:11,960 --> 00:43:13,960
now the fourth and final COPD

2236
00:43:13,960 --> 00:43:15,960
is actually bronchiectasis

2237
00:43:15,960 --> 00:43:17,960
what is bronchiectasis

2238
00:43:17,960 --> 00:43:18,960
this is a dilatation

2239
00:43:18,960 --> 00:43:19,960
of the bronchioles

2240
00:43:19,960 --> 00:43:20,960
and the bronchi

2241
00:43:20,960 --> 00:43:21,960
so these are the larger airways

2242
00:43:21,960 --> 00:43:23,960
and it's a loss of tone

2243
00:43:23,960 --> 00:43:24,960
that results in ear trapping

2244
00:43:24,960 --> 00:43:25,960
again let's explain

2245
00:43:25,960 --> 00:43:26,960
what happens in this

2246
00:43:26,960 --> 00:43:27,960
particular disease

2247
00:43:27,960 --> 00:43:28,960
is that the patient

2248
00:43:28,960 --> 00:43:29,960
has an airway

2249
00:43:29,960 --> 00:43:30,960
this is the normal

2250
00:43:30,960 --> 00:43:31,960
and when you have

2251
00:43:31,960 --> 00:43:32,960
these airways

2252
00:43:32,960 --> 00:43:33,960
the problem in bronchiectasis

2253
00:43:33,960 --> 00:43:34,960
is going to be that

2254
00:43:34,960 --> 00:43:35,960
you get abnormal dilation

2255
00:43:35,960 --> 00:43:36,960
of the airway

2256
00:43:36,960 --> 00:43:38,960
now when there's abnormal

2257
00:43:38,960 --> 00:43:40,960
dilation of these large airways

2258
00:43:40,960 --> 00:43:42,960
that results in loss of

2259
00:43:42,960 --> 00:43:43,960
airway tone

2260
00:43:43,960 --> 00:43:44,960
and air trapping

2261
00:43:44,960 --> 00:43:45,960
perhaps the easiest way

2262
00:43:45,960 --> 00:43:46,960
to understand this

2263
00:43:46,960 --> 00:43:47,960
is if I gave you a straw

2264
00:43:47,960 --> 00:43:48,960
and I asked you to blow

2265
00:43:48,960 --> 00:43:49,960
through the straw

2266
00:43:49,960 --> 00:43:50,960
and I put my hand

2267
00:43:50,960 --> 00:43:51,960
on the other side

2268
00:43:51,960 --> 00:43:52,960
I would clearly be able

2269
00:43:52,960 --> 00:43:53,960
to feel the air coming out

2270
00:43:53,960 --> 00:43:55,960
if I gave you a pipe

2271
00:43:55,960 --> 00:43:56,960
bigger than the size

2272
00:43:56,960 --> 00:43:57,960
of your face

2273
00:43:57,960 --> 00:43:58,960
and I asked you to blow out

2274
00:43:58,960 --> 00:44:00,960
I would not feel any air

2275
00:44:00,960 --> 00:44:01,960
coming out the other side

2276
00:44:01,960 --> 00:44:02,960
and that's because

2277
00:44:02,960 --> 00:44:03,960
as air would be accelerated

2278
00:44:03,960 --> 00:44:05,960
it would begin to sort of

2279
00:44:05,960 --> 00:44:06,960
just whirl around in this tube

2280
00:44:06,960 --> 00:44:07,960
and wouldn't be able

2281
00:44:07,960 --> 00:44:08,960
to be accelerated

2282
00:44:08,960 --> 00:44:09,960
out towards the other end

2283
00:44:09,960 --> 00:44:11,960
and that's exactly what happens

2284
00:44:11,960 --> 00:44:12,960
in bronchiectasis

2285
00:44:12,960 --> 00:44:15,960
this dilation of these airways

2286
00:44:15,960 --> 00:44:17,960
results in loss of tone

2287
00:44:17,960 --> 00:44:18,960
and that then results

2288
00:44:18,960 --> 00:44:19,960
in air trapping

2289
00:44:19,960 --> 00:44:20,960
so that when these patients

2290
00:44:20,960 --> 00:44:21,960
blow out

2291
00:44:21,960 --> 00:44:22,960
they can't get air out

2292
00:44:22,960 --> 00:44:23,960
appropriately

2293
00:44:23,960 --> 00:44:24,960
they're obstructed

2294
00:44:24,960 --> 00:44:25,960
from emptying the lung

2295
00:44:25,960 --> 00:44:26,960
here's a classic image

2296
00:44:26,960 --> 00:44:27,960
of bronchiectasis

2297
00:44:27,960 --> 00:44:28,960
and the idea here

2298
00:44:28,960 --> 00:44:29,960
is the following

2299
00:44:29,960 --> 00:44:30,960
when you look at the lung

2300
00:44:30,960 --> 00:44:31,960
you normally should see

2301
00:44:31,960 --> 00:44:32,960
some larger airways

2302
00:44:32,960 --> 00:44:33,960
in the center of the lung

2303
00:44:33,960 --> 00:44:34,960
because that's where

2304
00:44:34,960 --> 00:44:35,960
the large airways are

2305
00:44:35,960 --> 00:44:36,960
however when you come out

2306
00:44:36,960 --> 00:44:37,960
to the periphery

2307
00:44:37,960 --> 00:44:38,960
here is normal

2308
00:44:38,960 --> 00:44:40,960
you don't see those large airways

2309
00:44:40,960 --> 00:44:42,960
here is where the bronchiectasis is

2310
00:44:42,960 --> 00:44:43,960
and notice that

2311
00:44:43,960 --> 00:44:44,960
at the edge of the lung

2312
00:44:44,960 --> 00:44:45,960
I'm seeing these large

2313
00:44:45,960 --> 00:44:47,960
dilated circular air spaces

2314
00:44:47,960 --> 00:44:49,960
so that is classic bronchiectasis

2315
00:44:49,960 --> 00:44:51,960
the next question is

2316
00:44:51,960 --> 00:44:53,960
why do we get this

2317
00:44:53,960 --> 00:44:55,960
this dilatation of the airways

2318
00:44:55,960 --> 00:44:56,960
and the answer is

2319
00:44:56,960 --> 00:44:57,960
it's usually due to

2320
00:44:57,960 --> 00:44:59,960
necrotizing inflammation

2321
00:44:59,960 --> 00:45:00,960
with damage to the airway wall

2322
00:45:00,960 --> 00:45:01,960
so for example

2323
00:45:01,960 --> 00:45:03,960
this will occur in patients

2324
00:45:03,960 --> 00:45:04,960
who have some reason

2325
00:45:04,960 --> 00:45:06,960
to have chronic inflammation

2326
00:45:06,960 --> 00:45:07,960
and infection

2327
00:45:07,960 --> 00:45:08,960
within the airway

2328
00:45:08,960 --> 00:45:09,960
which is then going to result

2329
00:45:09,960 --> 00:45:11,960
in damage to the wall

2330
00:45:11,960 --> 00:45:13,960
which then dilates the airway

2331
00:45:13,960 --> 00:45:14,960
classic example

2332
00:45:14,960 --> 00:45:15,960
cystic fibrosis

2333
00:45:15,960 --> 00:45:17,960
you know that in cystic fibrosis

2334
00:45:17,960 --> 00:45:19,960
patients have thick secretions

2335
00:45:19,960 --> 00:45:20,960
the thick secretions

2336
00:45:20,960 --> 00:45:22,960
cause mucus plugging

2337
00:45:22,960 --> 00:45:23,960
the mucus plugging

2338
00:45:23,960 --> 00:45:24,960
increases the risk of infection

2339
00:45:24,960 --> 00:45:26,960
because you've blocked a tube

2340
00:45:26,960 --> 00:45:27,960
and when you get infection

2341
00:45:27,960 --> 00:45:28,960
you're going to get damage

2342
00:45:28,960 --> 00:45:29,960
to the airway

2343
00:45:29,960 --> 00:45:30,960
and so eventually

2344
00:45:30,960 --> 00:45:31,960
you're going to get bronchiectasis

2345
00:45:31,960 --> 00:45:33,960
and cystic fibrosis patients

2346
00:45:33,960 --> 00:45:35,960
classically have bronchiectasis

2347
00:45:35,960 --> 00:45:37,960
another case

2348
00:45:37,960 --> 00:45:38,960
where we might see this

2349
00:45:38,960 --> 00:45:39,960
is Cartagener syndrome

2350
00:45:39,960 --> 00:45:41,960
in Cartagener syndrome

2351
00:45:41,960 --> 00:45:42,960
the idea here

2352
00:45:42,960 --> 00:45:43,960
is that you have a defect

2353
00:45:43,960 --> 00:45:44,960
in what

2354
00:45:44,960 --> 00:45:45,960
I think every medical student

2355
00:45:45,960 --> 00:45:46,960
is usually able to say cilia

2356
00:45:46,960 --> 00:45:47,960
but you need to take it

2357
00:45:47,960 --> 00:45:48,960
one step further

2358
00:45:48,960 --> 00:45:49,960
what part of the cilia

2359
00:45:49,960 --> 00:45:50,960
is defective

2360
00:45:50,960 --> 00:45:52,960
ok it's the dianine arm

2361
00:45:52,960 --> 00:45:54,960
the dianine arm

2362
00:45:54,960 --> 00:45:55,960
which is one component

2363
00:45:55,960 --> 00:45:56,960
of the cilia

2364
00:45:56,960 --> 00:45:57,960
is defective

2365
00:45:57,960 --> 00:45:58,960
and that is necessary

2366
00:45:58,960 --> 00:46:00,960
for ciliary movement

2367
00:46:00,960 --> 00:46:02,960
so that's Cartagener syndrome

2368
00:46:02,960 --> 00:46:03,960
now where would be classic

2369
00:46:03,960 --> 00:46:04,960
what would be the symptoms

2370
00:46:04,960 --> 00:46:05,960
of this

2371
00:46:05,960 --> 00:46:06,960
you get sinusitis

2372
00:46:06,960 --> 00:46:07,960
because the cilia

2373
00:46:07,960 --> 00:46:08,960
of the respiratory epithelium

2374
00:46:08,960 --> 00:46:09,960
in the sinuses

2375
00:46:09,960 --> 00:46:10,960
is not functioning properly

2376
00:46:10,960 --> 00:46:12,960
so you get inflammation there

2377
00:46:12,960 --> 00:46:13,960
the patients get infertility

2378
00:46:13,960 --> 00:46:14,960
because the cilia of the sperm

2379
00:46:14,960 --> 00:46:16,960
is not functioning properly

2380
00:46:16,960 --> 00:46:17,960
they get something called

2381
00:46:17,960 --> 00:46:18,960
situs inverses

2382
00:46:18,960 --> 00:46:19,960
which is where

2383
00:46:19,960 --> 00:46:20,960
the organs that are normally

2384
00:46:20,960 --> 00:46:21,960
present on one side

2385
00:46:21,960 --> 00:46:22,960
of the thorax

2386
00:46:22,960 --> 00:46:23,960
are on the opposite side

2387
00:46:23,960 --> 00:46:24,960
so for example

2388
00:46:24,960 --> 00:46:25,960
the heart instead of being

2389
00:46:25,960 --> 00:46:26,960
on the left

2390
00:46:26,960 --> 00:46:27,960
is on the right side

2391
00:46:27,960 --> 00:46:28,960
so that's Cartagener syndrome

2392
00:46:28,960 --> 00:46:29,960
at the same time

2393
00:46:29,960 --> 00:46:30,960
they're going to get

2394
00:46:30,960 --> 00:46:31,960
inflammation

2395
00:46:31,960 --> 00:46:32,960
and infection

2396
00:46:32,960 --> 00:46:33,960
within the lung

2397
00:46:33,960 --> 00:46:34,960
and that's because

2398
00:46:34,960 --> 00:46:35,960
they don't have the cilia

2399
00:46:35,960 --> 00:46:36,960
to pump the mucus

2400
00:46:36,960 --> 00:46:37,960
out of the lung

2401
00:46:37,960 --> 00:46:38,960
to clear the lung

2402
00:46:38,960 --> 00:46:39,960
and so therefore

2403
00:46:39,960 --> 00:46:40,960
there's going to be

2404
00:46:40,960 --> 00:46:41,960
an increased risk of

2405
00:46:41,960 --> 00:46:42,960
infection and inflammation

2406
00:46:42,960 --> 00:46:43,960
so that's the second

2407
00:46:43,960 --> 00:46:44,960
classic patient

2408
00:46:44,960 --> 00:46:46,960
who might get bronchiectasis

2409
00:46:46,960 --> 00:46:47,960
a third patient

2410
00:46:47,960 --> 00:46:48,960
would be tumor

2411
00:46:48,960 --> 00:46:49,960
or foreign body

2412
00:46:49,960 --> 00:46:50,960
here's the airways

2413
00:46:50,960 --> 00:46:51,960
here's another airway

2414
00:46:51,960 --> 00:46:52,960
if there's a foreign body

2415
00:46:52,960 --> 00:46:53,960
in the airway

2416
00:46:53,960 --> 00:46:54,960
that's going to result

2417
00:46:54,960 --> 00:46:55,960
in inflammation

2418
00:46:55,960 --> 00:46:56,960
and infection down here

2419
00:46:56,960 --> 00:46:57,960
if there's a block

2420
00:46:57,960 --> 00:46:58,960
in the tumor

2421
00:46:58,960 --> 00:46:59,960
so that compresses

2422
00:46:59,960 --> 00:47:00,960
the airway

2423
00:47:00,960 --> 00:47:01,960
that would also increase

2424
00:47:01,960 --> 00:47:02,960
the risk of infection

2425
00:47:02,960 --> 00:47:03,960
and inflammation

2426
00:47:03,960 --> 00:47:04,960
any type of

2427
00:47:04,960 --> 00:47:05,960
necrotizing infection

2428
00:47:05,960 --> 00:47:06,960
if the patient

2429
00:47:06,960 --> 00:47:07,960
gets infected

2430
00:47:07,960 --> 00:47:08,960
with a bug

2431
00:47:08,960 --> 00:47:09,960
that is particularly

2432
00:47:09,960 --> 00:47:10,960
necrotizing

2433
00:47:10,960 --> 00:47:11,960
and virulent

2434
00:47:11,960 --> 00:47:12,960
that could result

2435
00:47:12,960 --> 00:47:13,960
in bronchiectasis

2436
